   "rule": "When the approved translation is already accurate, do not raise a finding that only swaps in a synonym or another equally valid wording. zh-TW reviewers have repeatedly rejected such rewrites as \"interchangeable\" or \"not better from original translation\". Examples: 報表 and 報告 are both acceptable for a crash \"report\" button. Different measure words (quantifiers) for permission items are also interchangeable. Rewording a remove-bookmark menu item or a \"recommended\" label gains nothing either. Still flag the translation when it actually changes or loses meaning, for example when an \"older than %S months\" condition is rendered as just \"%S months ago\". Also flag glossary violations and leftover untranslated English.",
